      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 136,
      "outputTokens": 1086,
      "costUsd": 0.009842,
      "pronunciationText": "The ruler is the standard deviation. For the snapper, sigma is four, so five centimetres is five over four, one point two five sigmas. For the perch, sigma is two point five, so four centimetres is four over two point five, one point six sigmas. That count is the zed score, or standardised score. Subtract the mean from the value, then divide by the standard deviation. It tells you how many standard deviations the value lies above or below the mean. A negative zed means below, positive means above. Both catches are above, and the perch is further out, because one point six sigmas is more than one point two five."
    },
