      "costUsd": 0.008338499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Zed scores also compare results from different groups. Alex scored seventy-two in Maths, where the mean was sixty and the standard deviation twelve. Blake scored sixty-eight in English, with mean fifty-five and standard deviation ten. Alex has the higher mark. But Alex's zed score is twelve over twelve, which is one. Blake's is thirteen over ten, one point three. So Blake did better relative to the cohort, because Blake's mark is further above its mean, measured in standard deviations. To justify a comparison, quote both zed scores."
