      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 178,
      "outputTokens": 1367,
      "costUsd": 0.012392,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the areas. Every normal curve becomes the same standard normal, so one table works for all of them. This table gives the probability that Z is less than zed, the area to the left, for positive zeds. For one point two five, go down to the row for one point two, then across to the column for zero point zero five. The entry is zero point eight nine four four. That's the area to the left, so the area beyond the snapper is one minus that, zero point one zero five six. At one point six, the table gives zero point nine four five two, so beyond the perch is zero point zero five four eight. Under these normal models, about one snapper in ten is at least that long, but only about one perch in eighteen. Further out means a smaller tail, so the perch is the more unusual catch."
    },
