      "pronunciationText": "This table has no negative zeds, and symmetry fixes that. A drink-bottle filling machine aims for five hundred millilitres, with sigma eight. A bottle with four ninety is ten below, so zed is minus one point two five. The area below minus one point two five matches the area above plus one point two five, the snapper's tail. So it's zero point one zero five six, and about ten point six percent of bottles fall below four ninety. Any negative zed works the same way: flip to the other side, then take one minus the table."
